  TR['CN-REG-0138'] = {
    "lawId": "CN-REG-0138",
    "sourceLang": "zh",
    "targetLang": "en",
    "engine": "llm",
    "model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash",
    "promptVersion": "calr-trans-v2",
    "translatedAt": "2026-10-14",
    "reviewed": "machine",
    "glossaryVersion": "calr-terms-2026-10-v2",
    "completenessNote": "逐条对译，共 19 条；条号与官方原文一一对应，未合并、未省略。",
    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "These Provisions are formulated in accordance with the Exit and Entry Administration Law of the People's Republic of China and other laws for the purposes of regulating exit and entry administration, safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting and entering the country, and upholding national sovereignty, security and development interests."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 2,
        "text": {
          "en": "The State establishes and improves the system for preventing security risks associated with the exit of Chinese citizens.\nThe competent departments of the State Council in charge of foreign affairs and of culture and tourism, and Chinese diplomatic missions abroad, shall, in light of the security situation of the countries and regions concerned, including war or armed conflict, public order, natural disasters, accidents and disasters, and infectious disease epidemics, promptly and publicly release overseas safety reminders and security risk alerts for tourist destinations.\nChinese citizens shall pay attention to overseas safety reminders and security risk alerts for tourist destinations and avoid travelling to or staying in high-risk countries or regions.\nWhen accepting and examining applications for exit and entry documents of Chinese citizens and conducting exit border inspection, the immigration administration shall, in accordance with notices issued by the relevant competent departments of the State Council, remind Chinese citizens preparing to travel to high-risk countries or regions to travel with caution or to closely follow the local security situation, to remain vigilant, to strengthen precautions and to pay attention to safety. Where Chinese citizens are preparing to travel to countries or regions with the highest risk level or where cases seriously endangering personal safety occur frequently, they shall be dissuaded from travelling there when necessary."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 2."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 3,
        "text": {
          "en": "The grounds on which persons exiting or entering the country apply for exit or entry, stay or residence shall be true and lawful.\nWhen verifying the identity of persons exiting or entering the country and the grounds for their applications, the immigration administration and the visa authorities may make inquiries about the relevant circumstances and require them to produce or provide relevant documents, materials, electronic data and other information, and such persons shall cooperate.\nWhere an entity or individual issues a letter of invitation or other application materials for a person exiting or entering the country, it or he shall be responsible for the authenticity of the contents of the invitation and the matters certified, and shall cooperate with the immigration administration and the visa authorities in verifying the relevant information.\nWhere a person exiting or entering the country provides false materials or makes false statements, the immigration administration and the visa authorities have the power to decide not to issue exit or entry documents to him or not to permit his exit or entry."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 3."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 4,
        "text": {
          "en": "Where a Chinese citizen is subjected to the administrative penalty of detention for fraudulently obtaining exit or entry documents or for exiting or entering the country illegally, the immigration administration may, in light of the circumstances of the violation and the need to prevent unlawful and criminal acts, decide that the citizen shall not be permitted to exit the country for a period of six months to three years from the date on which the penalty is executed.\nWhere a Chinese citizen engages in unlawful or criminal activities abroad that endanger national security and interests, the relevant competent department of the State Council may decide that the citizen shall not be permitted to exit the country for a period of six months to three years from the date of return to China, or, after verification by a Chinese diplomatic mission abroad, the provincial people's government of the place where the citizen is domiciled within China may make such a decision.\nWhere a Chinese citizen violates the provisions on export control, technology import and export administration or other such provisions in a manner that may endanger national industrial security or technological security, the competent departments of the State Council in charge of commerce and other relevant matters may decide that the citizen shall not be permitted to exit the country."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 4."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 5,
        "text": {
          "en": "Where a foreign national applies for a Chinese visa abroad or applies for entry at a port and provides false materials or makes false statements, the immigration administration or the visa authorities may decide that the foreign national shall not be permitted to enter the country for a period of one to five years.\nWhere a foreign national is subjected to a criminal penalty for obstructing the administration of the national border (frontier), or to an administrative penalty for fraudulently obtaining exit or entry documents or for exiting or entering the country illegally, the immigration administration may, in light of the circumstances of the violation and the need to prevent unlawful and criminal acts, decide that the foreign national shall not be permitted to enter the country for a period of one to five years from the date on which the penalty is executed. Where other laws provide otherwise, those provisions shall prevail.\nWhere a foreign national is included in a countermeasure list, an unreliable entity list or a malicious entity list, or is subjected to countermeasures and restrictive measures, and relevant measures such as not issuing exit or entry documents or not permitting entry need to be taken in accordance with law, the immigration administration and the visa authorities shall implement them in accordance with their duties."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 5."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 6,
        "text": {
          "en": "For a person whom it is decided in accordance with law not to permit to exit the country, the deciding organ shall, in accordance with the provisions, promptly notify the immigration administration for implementation and shall inform the person in writing of the facts, reasons, basis and remedies for not permitting exit; where such notification may affect national security, the investigation of a criminal case or other such circumstances, the person need not be informed.\nWhen implementing a decision not to permit exit, the immigration administration shall inform the person in accordance with the contents of the notice given by the deciding organ."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 6."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 7,
        "text": {
          "en": "The State applies record-filing administration to institutions and individuals that, entrusted by persons exiting or entering the country, provide intermediary services such as consulting on exit and entry policies, handling documents on their behalf and going through formalities.\nAn institution providing exit and entry intermediary services shall, within 15 days from the date of its establishment, file a record with the immigration administration of the place where it is located. Individuals providing exit and entry intermediary services shall have the record-filing formalities handled by the institution to which they belong. Those that were already providing exit and entry intermediary services before these Provisions came into force shall complete the record-filing formalities within 90 days from the date on which these Provisions come into force.\nThe specific measures for the record-filing administration of institutions and individuals providing exit and entry intermediary services shall be formulated by the national immigration administration department together with the competent departments of the State Council in charge of market regulation and other relevant matters."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 7."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 8,
        "text": {
          "en": "An institution providing exit and entry intermediary services shall meet the following conditions:\n(a) it is established in accordance with law;\n(b) its legal representative or person in charge has not been subjected to a criminal penalty for an intentional crime;\n(c) it has staff with professional knowledge of the laws, regulations and policies on exit and entry and other relevant fields, and has funds and premises appropriate to the intermediary service activities it engages in;\n(d) the staff who directly provide intermediary services to persons exiting or entering the country have not been subjected to a criminal penalty for an intentional crime endangering national security or public security or obstructing the administration of the national border (frontier);\n(e) it has sound management systems, including those for personnel management, education and training, record keeping, data security and compliance management.\nAn institution providing exit intermediary services shall also have established cooperative relations with the relevant service institutions outside China or signed a valid letter of intent for cooperation.\nOverseas enterprises and institutions shall not provide exit and entry intermediary services within China."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 8."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 9,
        "text": {
          "en": "The immigration administration shall, together with the competent departments at the same level in charge of foreign affairs, education, judicial administration, human resources and social security, commerce, culture and tourism, market regulation and other relevant matters, establish and improve the supervision system, strengthen, in accordance with the division of duties, supervision and administration over whether institutions providing exit and entry intermediary services meet the conditions and over their business activities, and publish the relevant information on violations and adverse records in accordance with law.\nThe competent departments concerned and their staff shall keep confidential, in accordance with law, the state secrets, work secrets, trade secrets, personal privacy and personal information that they learn of in the performance of their duties."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 9."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 10,
        "text": {
          "en": "An institution providing exit and entry intermediary services shall not commit any of the following acts:\n(a) publishing false information, or soliciting clients by exaggeration, misleading publicity or other such means;\n(b) providing or assisting in providing false materials, or assisting others in irregularly obtaining visas, stay or residence permits, passports or other exit or entry documents or formalities;\n(c) disclosing, selling or illegally providing trade secrets, personal privacy or personal information learned of in intermediary service activities;\n(d) providing exit and entry intermediary services beyond the scope recorded;\n(e) organising or assisting others in engaging in cross-border unlawful or criminal activities;\n(f) other acts endangering national security or interests or disrupting the order of exit and entry administration.\nWhere public officials, military personnel or other persons entrust an institution providing exit and entry intermediary services with irregularly obtaining foreign nationality, permanent residence status abroad, residence documents abroad or other exit or entry documents or formalities, the institution shall not handle the matter and shall promptly report to the supervisory organ and other relevant authorities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 10."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 11,
        "text": {
          "en": "Whoever obtains visas, stay or residence permits, passports or other exit or entry documents by fraud through providing false materials, making false statements or other such means shall be penalised by the immigration administration in accordance with the Exit and Entry Administration Law of the People's Republic of China and the Passport Law of the People's Republic of China.\nWhere an individual issues a false letter of invitation or other application materials for another person's application for exit or entry, stay or residence, the immigration administration shall impose a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 10,000; any illegal gains shall be confiscated. Where an entity commits the aforesaid act, it shall be fined not less than RMB 10,000 but not more than RMB 50,000; any illegal gains shall be confiscated; and a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 10,000 shall be imposed on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons. Where other laws provide otherwise, those provisions shall prevail."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 11."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 12,
        "text": {
          "en": "Where an institution providing exit and entry intermediary services violates Article 7 or Article 8 of these Provisions, the immigration administration shall order it to make correction within a specified time limit; where it refuses to make correction, a fine of not less than RMB 5,000 but not more than RMB 10,000 shall be imposed, and the competent department concerned shall be notified to order the suspension of the relevant business or the suspension of business for rectification; where the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 but not more than RMB 50,000 shall be imposed, and the competent department concerned shall be notified to revoke the relevant business licence or the business licence.\nWhere an individual provides exit and entry intermediary services in violation of these Provisions, the immigration administration shall order him to stop the unlawful act; any illegal gains shall be confiscated; where the circumstances are serious, a fine of not more than RMB 5,000 may also be imposed."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 12."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 13,
        "text": {
          "en": "Where an institution providing exit and entry intermediary services violates Article 10 of these Provisions and disrupts the order of exit and entry administration, the immigration administration shall order it to make correction within a specified time limit; any illegal gains shall be confiscated; where the illegal gains are RMB 20,000 or more, a fine of not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains shall also be imposed; where there are no illegal gains or the illegal gains are less than RMB 20,000, a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 but not more than RMB 50,000 shall also be imposed; where it refuses to make correction or the circumstances are serious, the competent department concerned shall be notified to order the suspension of the relevant business, the suspension of business for rectification, the revocation of the relevant business licence or the revocation of the business licence; and a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 but not more than RMB 50,000 shall be imposed on the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons. Where other laws provide otherwise, those provisions shall prevail."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 13."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 14,
        "text": {
          "en": "Where the exit and entry administration of the public security organ of a local people's government at or above the county level imposes, in accordance with these Provisions, an administrative penalty of a fine exceeding RMB 5,000 or of confiscation of illegal gains, the decision shall be made by the public security organ to which it belongs."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 14."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 15,
        "text": {
          "en": "The relevant competent departments of the State Council shall strengthen coordination in safeguarding the lawful rights and interests of persons exiting or entering the country, preventing security risks associated with the exit of Chinese citizens, and administering exit and entry intermediary services."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 15."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 16,
        "text": {
          "en": "The immigration administration shall keep open the channels for reporting acts violating exit and entry administration and shall handle the reports promptly in accordance with law. Reports that do not fall within its own duties shall be promptly referred to the relevant entity for handling in accordance with law."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 16."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 17,
        "text": {
          "en": "Whoever violates these Provisions and thereby commits a crime shall be investigated for criminal responsibility in accordance with law."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 17."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 18,
        "text": {
          "en": "For the purposes of these Provisions, the immigration administration means the national immigration administration department, the exit and entry border inspection authorities, and the exit and entry administration of the public security organs of local people's governments at or above the county level.\nFor the purposes of these Provisions, the visa authorities mean the visa authorities stationed abroad and the port visa authorities."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 18."
        }
      },
      {
        "no": 19,
        "text": {
          "en": "These Provisions come into force on 15 September 2026."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 19."
        }
      }
    ]
  };

